        <!-- Closing -->
        <div class="mt-16 bg-gray-900 text-white rounded-2xl p-8">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Milwaukee and DeWalt both make professional-grade cordless tools that will serve a homeowner for a decade and a tradesperson for years of daily use. Milwaukee wins on breadth of specialty tools, the compact M12 line and a longer standard warranty. DeWalt wins on retail availability, FLEXVOLT high-power saws, frequent bundle deals and its satisfaction guarantee.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Pick the platform whose next five tools match your work, then stay with it. That decision will save more money and frustration than any spec sheet comparison. If your needs are lighter, a budget platform may be the smarter buy, and either way, pair your cordless kit with quality hand tools and a calibrated torque wrench for jobs that need precision.
          </p>
